390
00:17:03,460 --> 00:17:05,349
To close things off
here, I have with me

391
00:17:05,349 --> 00:17:08,140
Lisha Lee, who did her PhD
work on the theoretical side

392
00:17:08,140 --> 00:17:09,579
of deep learning
and who currently

393
00:17:09,579 --> 00:17:12,460
works at a venture capital firm
called Amplify Partners, who

394
00:17:12,460 --> 00:17:15,010
kindly provided some of
the funding for this video.

395
00:17:15,010 --> 00:17:17,770
So, Lisha, one thing I think
we should quickly bring up

396
00:17:17,770 --> 00:17:19,490
is this sigmoid function.

397
00:17:19,490 --> 00:17:20,920
As I understand
it, early networks

398
00:17:20,920 --> 00:17:23,050
use this to squish the
relevant weighted sum

399
00:17:23,050 --> 00:17:25,450
into that interval
between 0 and 1,

400
00:17:25,450 --> 00:17:28,339
kind of motivated by this
biological analogy of neurons

401
00:17:28,339 --> 00:17:29,678
either being inactive or active.

402
00:17:29,678 --> 00:17:30,470
LISHA LEE: Exactly.

403
00:17:30,470 --> 00:17:32,660
INSTRUCTOR: But relatively
few modern networks

404
00:17:32,660 --> 00:17:34,280
actually use sigmoid anymore.

405
00:17:34,280 --> 00:17:35,790
That's kind of
old school, right?

406
00:17:35,790 --> 00:17:39,153
LISHA LEE: Or rather, ReLU seems
to be much easier to train.

407
00:17:39,153 --> 00:17:40,070
INSTRUCTOR: And ReLU--

408
00:17:40,070 --> 00:17:42,630
ReLU stands for
Rectified Linear Unit.

409
00:17:42,630 --> 00:17:44,570
LISHA LEE: Yes, it's
this kind of function

410
00:17:44,570 --> 00:17:47,690
where you're just taking
a max of 0 and a, where

411
00:17:47,690 --> 00:17:51,270
a is given by what you were
explaining in the video.

412
00:17:51,270 --> 00:17:53,330
And what this was sort
of motivated from,

413
00:17:53,330 --> 00:17:57,290
I think was partially
by a biological analogy

414
00:17:57,290 --> 00:18:01,560
with how neurons would
either be activated or not.

415
00:18:01,560 --> 00:18:03,740
And so if it passes
a certain threshold,

416
00:18:03,740 --> 00:18:05,730
it would be the
identity function.

417
00:18:05,730 --> 00:18:09,000
But if it did not, then it
would just not be activated.

418
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:09,690
So it'd be 0.

419
00:18:09,690 --> 00:18:11,130
So it's kind of
a simplification.

420
00:18:11,130 --> 00:18:13,160
Using sigmoids
didn't help training,

421
00:18:13,160 --> 00:18:15,710
or it was very difficult
to train at some point.

422
00:18:15,710 --> 00:18:17,870
And people just tried ReLU.

423
00:18:17,870 --> 00:18:23,810
And it happened to work very
well for these incredibly deep

424
00:18:23,810 --> 00:18:24,523
neural networks.

425
00:18:24,523 --> 00:18:25,440
INSTRUCTOR: All right.

426
